{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/129631-fantasy-grounds-virtual-table-top-now-available-on-steam-and-w-promotional-weekend","id":129631,"title":"Fantasy Grounds Virtual Table Top now available on steam and w/ promotional weekend","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-09T22:33:54-07:00","id":129631,"title":"Fantasy Grounds Virtual Table Top now available on steam and w/ promotional weekend","content":"If, like me, you've been too busy to meet regularly (you know, in the 3d world) to do - that voodoo - that we do, so well then you've probably been looking for a good VTT to help fill in the gaps. Now, I haven't used Fantasy Grounds myself (except the demo once for the dice roller) but it comes well ranked and recommended. It seems they've recently launched through steam, and to celebrate have made the demo fully functional in addition to discounting the product.<br /> <br /> It would seem that the community made its own <a href=\"http://www.fantasygrounds.com/wiki/index.php?title=Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">Nwod + Masq rulesets</a>, and again I haven't used them, but if you've ever been tempted to try FG or VTTs in general, then now's probably a good chance to kick the tires.<br /> <br /> Anyways, happy gaming and I'll see you out in the mists of Morpheus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1770-dream_asylum","name":"Dream_Asylum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T01:01:49-07:00","id":129708,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://app.roll20.net/home\" target=\"_blank\">Roll20</a> is another great VTT product to check out, and it is free (with sub options for luxury functions). This is the one I usually suggest for folks new to VTT, as they can check it out without spending anything.<br /> <br /> Also check out <a href=\"http://www.infrno.net/base/welcome\" target=\"_blank\">Infrno</a> and <a href=\"http://www.rptools.net/index.php?page=maptool\" target=\"_blank\">MapTools</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T13:14:24-07:00","id":139672,"title":"","content":"To me, Roll20 is either far more than I need as I'm not use a battle map and skype would be enough, or I want more functions than it have. So I have bought Fantasy Grounds as I believe it will fit what I want.<br /> <br /> The strength of Fantasy Grounds is also the drawback. It is extensively modifyable through XML and Lua, so it can do a lot of calculations in the background. Some apparently use it even in face to face games to do the book keeping of character, NPC, items and the story. But if no one already have made what one need, it can be a daunting task to make those modifications (there is currently a crowd funder for development of some tools to make it easier).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}